.Dd February 11, 2026
.Dt VOP_WRITE 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vop_write
.Nd write data from a uio into a vnode
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/uio.h
.In vfs/vnode.h
.Ft int
.Fn vop_write "struct vnode *vp" "struct uio *uio" "int ioflag" "struct ucred *cred"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn vop_write
validates write requests, honors append mode by writing at end-of-file,
delegates to the filesystem callback, updates vnode size when writes extend the
file, and marks modification state.
If
.Dv IO_SYNC
is present, data is synchronously flushed via
.Fn vop_fsync .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success, or an error number.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EOPNOTSUPP]"
.It Bq Er EINVAL
Invalid uio descriptor.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The vnode does not implement write.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vnode 9 ,
.Xr vop_read 9 ,
.Xr vop_fsync 9
